  "description": "Immediate-mode vector shapes for Stride: filled convex shapes whose outline stays a constant few pixels wide at any zoom, distance or window size, because a signed distance function measures it per fragment instead of building it as geometry.\n\nWhat's inside:\n- ShapeBatch, registered with game.AddShapeBatch(): polygons, discs, rings, rounded rectangles, wire boxes, camera-facing billboards, and 3D lines in either a real world-space width or a constant on-screen pixel width, where hardware line rendering clamps to one pixel\n- Flat shapes placed anywhere in 3D - on a plane you choose, facing the camera, or swung about an axis - as well as the plain 2D case\n- Thousands of shapes per frame in one instanced draw call: no models, materials or assets involved\n- ShapeComponent to draw a shape from an entity's transform, so shapes join the component system without needing a model\n- Per-shape outline width and fill, and per-batch depth testing for scene decals versus overlay gizmos\n\nPorted from the Box2D testbed's solid_polygon shader (Erin Catto, MIT) and extended to 3D.\n\nStride compatibility (each toolkit version is built for one Stride release):\n- Stride 4.4: this version\n- Stride 4.3: 1.0.0-preview.62\n- Stride 4.2: 1.0.0-preview.61\n\nDocumentation: https://stride3d.github.io/stride-community-toolkit/\nSource and 50+ runnable examples: https://github.com/stride3d/stride-community-toolkit",
